{
 "name": "wheg6",
 "description": "One-shaft synchronous wheg climber: a single lengthwise shaft (axles joined by 32034 connectors) with a worm over each 40T wheel gear gives all four 3-spoke whegs one crank angle, so front and rear spokes stay parallel and the body climbs as a parallelogram at the stair slope (264 mm wheelbase, 256 mm treads). In-line XL motor at the nose, high above the risers; AA box over the nose so motor torque cannot wheelie the body; spokes 140 mm (1.33 x riser), started 18 deg forward so the tips land on the treads; worms self-lock against rollback.",
